  "rationale": "Class 2 row-level check. X06 fired because principal_amount_usd is more than 10x fair_value, but the SOI source rows themselves show the same par/principal amounts and low fair values in the Par Amount/Units, Cost, and Fair Value columns. The flagged condition is therefore not a scale or FX extraction error for the localized rows; it is a rule-scope false alarm on valid low-fair-value debt/commitment rows. Seven of nine flagged row values were directly localized in source; the remaining two were not independently localized within the targeted evidence budget, so confidence is below high."
